      "text": "1. **Identify Total Players and Selected Players:**\n   Coach Grunt needs to choose a lineup of 5 players from the 12 on the team, given that Ace and Zeppo must be in the lineup.\n   - Total players: \\(12\\)\n   - Selected players: \\(2\\) (Ace and Zeppo) + \\(3\\) (additional players)\n\n2. **Calculate Number of Ways to Choose Additional Players:**\n   We need to select 3 more players from the remaining \\(12 - 2 = 10\\) players on the team.\n   - The number of ways to choose 3 players from 10 is given by the combination formula \\( \\binom{n}{k} \\), where \\(n\\) is the total number of items to choose from, and \\(k\\) is the number of items to choose.\n   \\[\n   \\binom{10}{3} = \\frac{10!}{3!(10-3)!} = \\frac{10!}{3! \\cdot 7!}\n   \\]\n   \n3. **Simplify the Combination:**\n   \\[\n   \\binom{10}{3} = \\frac{10 \\times 9 \\times 8}{3 \\times 2 \\times 1} = \\frac{720}{6} = 120\n   \\]\n\n4. **Calculate Total Number of Lineup Combinations:**\n   Since Ace and Zeppo are fixed in the lineup, we only need the number of ways to arrange the 3 additional players in the lineup.\n   - The number of ways to arrange 3 players in a lineup is given by the permutation formula \\( P(n, k) \\), where \\(n\\) is the total number of items to arrange from, and \\(k\\) is the number of items to arrange.\n   \\[\n   P(3, 3) = 3! = 3 \\times 2 \\times 1 = 6\n   \\]\n\n5. **Combine the Results:**\n   The total number of different starting lineups is the product of the number of ways to choose the additional players and the number of ways to arrange them in the lineup.\n   \\[\n   120 \\times 6 = 720\n   \\]\n\n### Conclusion:\nThe number of different starting lineups possible is \\(\\boxed{720}\\).",
